Z||000000||Monkeyman||02-05-2001||06:00 PM||||As I said in my sensor thread (which I can't seem to find right now), my ECM is throwing some codes (13, 21, 24, 25, &32).  Yesterday I replaced the TPS sensor with no change.  (It was rainy today (hence wet) and the car still idled and ran like crap.)  Today I replaced the MAT sensor & EGR solenoid.  Suddenly, the check engine light isn't on.  The bulb doesn't look blown (interesting time to blow, if it did) and I don't have another tonight.  Is it possible that I actually fixed the problem?  Isn't the light supposed to stay on until you reset the ECM even if you fix the problem??  I know that the O2 sensor should still throw a code.  I should probably make a quick trip to Autozone for a replacement bulb, but I'm not in any condition to drive.<P>Have I encountered another Fiero gremlin, this time a good one?<P>Is this all just a bad dream?  Will I wake up and find that everything is OK?  (I would say back to normal, but... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">)<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||02-05-2001||06:06 PM||||The ECM light is on when the ECM sees an error. The light usually goes off unless the error is a hard problem.<P>Don't forget sensors are all related. any one goofing off can throw a bunch of errors.<P>If the bulb is blown it won't light durring starting or when you jumper the aldl....<P>At this point you need to fix the light if need be and reset the ECM. then see what if any errors return.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Monkeyman||02-05-2001||06:15 PM||||I'll be sure to swap bulbs tomorrow just to be sure.  The light usually doesn't come on until 30 seconds or so after the motor's been started.  It's never come on in any self diagnostic mode kind of thing.  Could you define a "hard problem"?  I know for sure that the O2 sensor should still be throwing a code since it's missing.  Maybe it'll rain tomorrow.  Since the car only has problems when it's wet, if it rains/snows and the car runs well, I've fixed the problem.  (Although I'm not counting on it.)||||reg||1
Z||000003||DRH||02-05-2001||06:48 PM||||The light should come on when you turn the ignition ON without starting it. This will tell you if the bulb is good.<P>Most codes will not make the light come on immediately when the car is started. It takes time for the computer to "notice" something is wrong. It won't set the O2 sensor code until the car warms up. It won't set the VSS code until it sees conditions (not in park, RPM = x, vacuum = y, etc...) that makes it "think" you must be driving down the road and it's getting nothing from the VSS. The TPS codes may set a little quicker.<P>Codes are stored until the ECM is reset, but most won't make the light come on again unless the problem happens again. There are a couple of exceptions which ogre refered to as hard codes. i don't think any you listed fall into that catagory.||||reg||1
Z||000004||oneof547||02-06-2001||10:27 AM||||To eliminate the blown bulb possibility COMPLETELY, jumper the ECM into Diagnostic mode, if the bulb does not flash at all its toast. You will feel and hear the car go into diagnostic mode, I.E. lower idle.<BR>Also for shits and giggles check out your coolant temp sensor wires, connections, and sensor it self. They  were all suspect to causing "gremlins" in mine. Once I replaced the sensor and shorted wire the car got its Balls and mileage back.<P>------------------<BR>oneof547<p>[This message has been edited by oneof547 (edited 02-06-2001).]||||reg||5
Z||000005||Monkeyman||02-06-2001||11:41 PM||||Noticed this am that the bulb does indeed come on in a diagnostic mode just after I hit the key.  My bad.<P>I've replaced all of the above except the O2 sensor (waiting on a new crossover).  Unfortunately, my original problem still exists.  It runs/idles terrible whenever it's wet out.  Must be electrical since it only happens when it's wet, right?  Could the fact that either the O2 sensor or the wire it attaches to is hanging in the open and getting wet?  Or would I have to have a bare wire somewhere?  I'm baffled and frustrated. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||1
